          %p
            In more detail, an
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              \-category
            consists of the following data:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %li
              %p
                for each pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
                of objects, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x,y)
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    loose
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %li
              %p
                for each pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
                of objects, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(x,y)
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x,y)
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong tight morphisms
            %li
              %p
                for each object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_x
            %li
              %p
                for each triple
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y, z
                of objects, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+operation"} binary operation
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∘
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ_{x,y,z}
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(y,z)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x,y)
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x,z)
                such that:
              %ul
                %li
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g
                  is tight whenever
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g
                  are;
                %li
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                          %mi y
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \id_y \circ f = f = f \circ \id_x
                  whenever this makes sense; and
                %li
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi h
                        %mo =
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi h
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f \circ g) \circ h = f \circ (g \circ h)
                  whenever this makes sense.
          %p
            Equivalently, an
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              \-category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of objects and
            %strong loose
            morphisms together with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
            of
            %strong tight
            morphisms.
          %p
            Note that the “underlying ordinary category” of an
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory, is its category of
            %em tight
            morphisms. This is because the underlying ordinary category is induced by a monoidal change-of-base functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(I, -) \colon \mathcal{M} \to Set
            represented by the monoidal unit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = (1, 1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi T
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom_{\mathcal{M}}((1, 1), (T, L)) \cong T.
          %p
            Nevertheless, it is frequently also useful to think of the category of loose morphisms as a sort of “underlying ordinary category” of an
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom_{\mathcal{M}}((0, 1), -) \colon \mathcal{M} \to Set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi L
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom_{\mathcal{M}}((0, 1), (T, L)) \cong L.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo †
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger-category"} category
                is an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+isomorphisms"} unitary isomorphisms
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
                form an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
                as tight morphisms.
            %li
              %p
                A more interesting way to make Hilbert spaces into an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilb"} Hilb
                uses (as in the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo †
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hilb
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hilb
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+operators"} bounded linear operators
                as loose morphisms but only
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+linear+operators"} short linear operators
                (those with norm at most
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo †
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dagger
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hilb
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hilb
                (but also has non-invertible tight morphisms).
            %li
              %p
                Similarly,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ban"} Ban
                (the category of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ban
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ban
                is traditionally called an ‘
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm+isomorphism"}> isomorphism
                ’ while a tight isomorphism is called a ‘
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+isometry"}> global isometry
                ’.
            %li
              %p
                We can make
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Met"} Met
                (the category of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+maps"} short maps
                contained in
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lipschitz+map"} Lipschitz map
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+continuous+maps"} uniformly continuous maps
                contained in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+maps"} bounded maps
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
                is an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equalities
                as the tight morphisms. (Thus the wide subcategory of tight morphisms is
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeletal+category"} skeletal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
                (or any category) in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
                is an
                = succeed "-category." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %li
              %p
                A more interesting way to make
                = succeed "'s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
                into an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                inclusions as tight morphisms. Again the tight isomorphisms are simply the equalities.
            %li
              %p
                Given any category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                form an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                on the subobjects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                and whose category of tight morphisms is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+poset"} subobject poset
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %li
              %p
                Similarly,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+objects"} quotient objects
                form an
                = succeed "-category." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                of every category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and whose tight morphisms are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                itself is an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
                for any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %li
              %p
                Given any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C \to D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                into an
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and whose loose morphisms from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                are the
                = succeed "-morphisms" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(x)
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(y)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                be a strict 2-monad on a strict 2-category. Then the strict
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \mathrm{Alg}
                where tight morphisms are the strict algebra morphisms and the loose morphisms are the pseudo algebra morphsims. This is just a decategorified version of the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℱ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
                = succeed "-algebras," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %p
                More generally, any strict
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℱ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
          %h2#applications Applications
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
                can be made into a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
                in a canonical way: declare two objects to be equal if they are
                %em tightly
                isomorphic. This is an unusual sort of strict category in that its “equality predicate” on objects may not be literal equality (even in a foundational system where the latter makes sense). Many strict categories that arise in practice underlie
                = succeed "-categories," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              %p
                Note that two
                %em equivalent
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %em isomorphic
                underlying strict categories (in the appropriate sense, i.e. making use of the stipulated equality predicate on objects to define “isomorphism”). In this way, some examples which may seem on the surface to violate the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
                by recognizing the presence of a neglected
                = succeed "-enrichment." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %li
              %p
                For instance, let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi Gal
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Gal(E/F)
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
                of a finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+extension"} Galois extension
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E/F
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\subset K\subset E
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                pointwise, and whose tight maps are those which commute with the inclusions into
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbits"} orbits
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
                = succeed "-sets," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
                says that these two
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    as
                    = succeed "-categories" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℳ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              %p
                This is a stronger statement than saying that their underlying strict categories, as above, are isomorphic, which is yet stronger than saying that their underlying categories of loose maps are equivalent. See
                %a{:href => "http://article.gmane.org/gmane.science.mathematics.categories/5877"} this post
                (
                %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/20150326125356/http://article.gmane.org/gmane.science.mathematics.categories/5877"}> archive
                ) by
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
